    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Soil starts as rock! Rain, wind and ice break rocks into tiny bits, over a very long time.",
      "punch": "tiny",
      "board": {
        "type": "lifecycle",
        "title": "Rock to soil",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🪨",
            "label": "Rock",
            "cue": "rock"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🧊",
            "label": "Breaks up",
            "cue": "break"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🟤",
            "label": "Tiny bits",
            "cue": "tiny"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⏳",
            "label": "Long time",
            "cue": "long"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So soil is just crushed rock?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Not just rock! It also has humus: old leaves and plants, all broken down.",
      "punch": "humus",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🍂",
        "text": "Plus humus",
        "cue": "humus",
        "sub": "Old leaves and plants",
        "sub_cue": "leaves"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Who mixes it all together?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Earthworms help! They mix the soil and dig tunnels, so air and water can get in.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🪱",
        "text": "Worms mix soil",
        "cue": "earthworms",
        "sub": "Tunnels for air",
        "sub_cue": "tunnels"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Then why isn't all soil the same?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Different rocks make different bits! Bigger bits make sand. Super tiny bits make clay.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🪨",
        "text": "Different rocks",
        "cue": "different",
        "sub": "Sand or clay",
        "sub_cue": "sand"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What's the difference?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Sandy soil is gritty, and water runs through fast. Clay soil is sticky and holds water.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Sandy",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Gritty",
              "icon": "🏖️",
              "cue": "gritty"
            },
            {
              "text": "Drains fast",
              "icon": "💨",
              "cue": "fast"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Clay",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Sticky",
              "icon": "🤏",
              "cue": "sticky"
            },
            {
              "text": "Holds water",
              "icon": "💧",
              "cue": "holds"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Is there soil in the middle?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yes! Loam is a good mix of sand, clay and humus. Lots of plants love it!",
